{{/*
Who git trusts to have signed a commit locally. It holds exactly the live
identities: no retired key is carried, because an ssh signature embeds the signer's public
key and a dropped line is reconstructible from any commit it signed (ADR 0008). Because
nothing accumulates here, no pruning rule has to exist.

Three lines against two keys (ADR 0011). Personal and company run through one github.com
account and therefore share its key, differing by address alone, so the same public key
appears twice under two addresses; the client-issued identity has its own account and its
own key.

Each line derives its key from the public key *file* rather than transcribing the blob a
second time — the two cleartext ones from the file in this repository, the client-issued
one from the same 1Password field ~/.ssh/id_work.pub renders from.
*/ -}}
{{- $personal := trim (include "private_dot_ssh/id_personal.pub") -}}
